7. YOUR MODIFICATIONS MUST GO BACK TO THE COMMUNITY

This project is shared on the understanding that improvements return to
everyone who uses it.

If you Distribute a Modification, then within thirty (30) days of first doing
so you must make the complete corresponding source code of that Modification
publicly available, free of charge, in a form a competent developer can build
and use, under this same licence, and you must tell recipients where to find
it.

Publishing that source in a public repository, or submitting it to us as a
pull request that we accept, satisfies this obligation.

This obligation is triggered only by Distribution. Modifications you make and
keep to yourself under Section 4 do not have to be published — though we hope
you will send them anyway.


